      "A 2001 constitutional reform introduced a rotating presidency among the three islands to manage separatist tensions; Azali Assoumani, in power intermittently since a 1999 coup, has served continuously as president since 2016, most recently securing another term via 2024 elections that opposition figures characterized as flawed."
